config HISI_ISP_REMOTEPROC
	tristate "Hisilicon ISP remote processor"
	depends on ARCH_HISI || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on REMOTEPROC
	depends on OF
	depends on IOMMU_SUPPORT
	select IOMMU_IO_PGTABLE_LPAE
	help
	  Say y here to support the Hisilicon Hi3670 ISP remote processor.

	  This is a mainline-style remoteproc driver.  It registers the ISP
	  Cortex-A7 with the remoteproc framework, maps the ISP register
	  windows, owns a local LPAE page table for the ISP SMMU and can load
	  an ELF firmware into on-demand mapped IOVA.

	  Optional clocks and regulators, the CRG remap bit and the ISP SMMU
	  registers are wired up.  The DT clock provider/supply wiring, secure
	  memory, shared memory and the mailbox/rpmsg transport are not ported
	  yet, so the remote processor cannot be booted.  Keep the DT node
	  disabled until those pieces land.
